Design inspirations (no code copied)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EQ Legends Companion
https://jmoyers.github.io/everquest-companion (product)
https://github.com/jmoyers/everquest-companion (source)
by Josh Moyers

Two alert-polish behaviors in EQBuddy follow designs we first saw in EQ Legends
Companion's source (its FSL-1.1-MIT license does not permit code use in a
competing product, and none was used — EQBuddy's implementations in
src/EQBuddy.UI.Shared/AlertThrottle.cs were written independently):

  - Alert cooldowns scoped per matched label, so the same rule firing on a
    DIFFERENT mob is not silenced by the cooldown from the previous one.
  - A sound gate where the first alert sound in a short window wins and plays
    to completion, instead of overlapping alerts cutting each other off.

Good designs deserve naming their source. Thanks, Josh.
